# Declaration only (spec 21 section 6, spec 25): games.tictactoe keeps its own patterns and operations. This schema serves the dice, the example chips and the action buttons (std.sample):
# the whole sentences the dice may say are read from the world's own state by the hook `sampleKnowledge` of ops.mjs (declaredExecutor). Nothing is generated except schema.declared.mjs.
@ttt acts.schema
    noun="move"
    declare=yes
    doc="Tic-tac-toe: the moves the user may play now (the free cells)."
    acts=make

@ttt.move acts.kind
    know=moves:*
    dice.not=make
    plural=moves
